    {
      "id": 326,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -460,
        60
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        900
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 32,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: source-video de-roping [alpha]",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## De-rope footage you already have  [ALPHA]\n\nNew 2026-08-12. The classic pipeline nodes are unchanged; only the front of the graph is different.\n\nInstead of rendering a baseline, this graph loads a file and encodes it. `H3 Jerk Oracle` reads that latent directly, and everything after it (smear, V2V init, inject, sample, exact recover, audio recover) is the standard pipeline.\n\n### Set these three before you queue\n\n1. **Load Video** -> your file. Anything ComfyUI can decode.\n2. **canvas** (ResolutionSelector) -> the aspect ratio of YOUR footage. The frames are centre-cropped to it, and the same width/height feed the conditioning.\n3. **prompt** -> describe your clip. The placeholder text says what each section is for. The sharpness clause at the end is the part that does the de-roping.\n\n### Why H3 Video Fit is in the chain\n\nH3 works in 17-frame chunks, so legal lengths are 5, 22, 39 ... 17k+5. An arbitrary file lands between them and **nothing errors**: the VAE pads the last chunk by repeating the final frame, so a 312-frame clip encodes as 323 with 11 frozen frames on the end, and the oracle reads that stillness as calm. The fit node trims to 311 instead and hands the count to the oracle's `length`. Read its report (the fit report preview node).\n\n`max_frames` is the cost lever: time per step goes as tokens**1.7, so capping a long source is the cheapest knob here. 0 = whole clip.\n\n### Audio\n\nYour own track is kept: `H3 Audio Recover` `reference_mix 1.0`. Exact recovery restores the world clock frame for frame, so the source audio still lines up. Lower the mix to hear the model's own foley instead. **If your source has no audio stream, delete that reference link** or the graph will fail on an empty AUDIO.\n"
      ]
    },
